    "status": "PASS",
    "source": "Same quantities on both sides: computed, whether ComputeNormals ran on at least one triangulated face; faces_with_normals_before and faces_with_normals_after, how many of the box's 6 faces carry normals; nodes_per_face; and max_plane_deviation, the largest | |n . plane| - 1 | over every node normal n against the plane normal of the face's first triangle (0 means every node normal is perpendicular to its face's plane). Bridge: on Shape.box(10, 10, 10) meshed with linearDeflection 0.1, Shape.triangulationHasNormals over the 6 faces read 0 before and 6 after Shape.computeNormals() (which returned true), each face has 4 nodes, and every triangulationNormal(at:) is the axis-aligned normal of its face (x for faces 0 and 1, y for 2 and 3, z for 4 and 5) with plane deviation 0.0 (temporary print of the rewritten test's values, not committed). Kernel: BRepMesh_IncrementalMesh(0.1, false, 0.5) on the same box, then BRepLib_ToolTriangulatedShape::ComputeNormals on every face, printed 'before: faces 6 withNormals 0', 'ComputeNormals ran on 6 faces, computed=1' and 'after: faces 6 withNormals 6 nodesPerFace 4..4 maxPlaneDeviation 0', with the same per-face normals (transcript-evidence-fix.txt). The sign of a node normal follows the surface, not the face's orientation, so faces 0 and 1 both carry +x; the test asserts the plane and not the sign. A gp_Dir is unit by construction, so unit length is not compared.",
    "probe": "Scripts/repro/766-topology-breplib-builders/transcript-evidence-fix.txt",
    "test_file": "Tests/OCCTTopologyTests/BRepLibToolTriangulatedShapeTests.swift",
    "injection": "I1: ComputeNormals never called (the function still returns true); I2: ComputeNormals on the first face only; I3: node 1's normal overwritten with (1, 1, 0); I5: meshing already computes the normals",
    "red": "BRepLibToolTriangulatedShapeTests.swift:32 face.triangulationHasNormals (I1: 6 issues, I2: 5) and :41 abs(abs(simd_dot(n, plane)) - 1) < 1e-12 (I1: 24, I2: 20, I3: 6); :26 !face.triangulationHasNormals (I5: 6)",
    "green": "passed",
